pokeplatinum-animctx.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): the overworld anim manager's
function context buffer (funcsCtx, inline in each manager) sized for the host. On the DS it is 160 bytes and every
manager's context struct fits (the Eterna gym's fountain animation uses 132); with 8-byte pointers the same struct is
224 bytes, so ResetFuncsContext's memset and the init function's writes ran past the buffer over the manager's own
init/tick/render/exit pointers (and into the next manager): the gym's anim tick then called a null pointer the frame
the player entered the gym (zone 67), SIGSEGV in OverworldAnimManager_CallTickFunc. 512 holds the host layout of
every context seen (the lists are 32 to 128 managers: at most ~80 KB). The assert says when a context ever outgrows it.

--- a/include/overworld_anim_manager.h
+++ b/include/overworld_anim_manager.h
@@ -7,5 +7,5 @@
 #include "sys_task.h"
 
-#define OVERWORLD_ANIM_MANAGER_FUNCS_CONTEXT_SIZE 160
+#define OVERWORLD_ANIM_MANAGER_FUNCS_CONTEXT_SIZE 512
 
 typedef struct OverworldAnimManager OverworldAnimManager;
--- a/src/overworld_anim_manager.c
+++ b/src/overworld_anim_manager.c
@@ -77,6 +77,7 @@
         OverworldAnimManager_SetPosition(iter, &zeroPos);
     }
 
+    GF_ASSERT(funcs->baseFuncs.ctxSize <= OVERWORLD_ANIM_MANAGER_FUNCS_CONTEXT_SIZE);
     OverworldAnimManager_ResetFuncsContext(iter, funcs->baseFuncs.ctxSize);
     OverworldAnimManager_SetInitFunc(iter, funcs->baseFuncs.initFunc);
     OverworldAnimManager_SetExitFunc(iter, funcs->baseFuncs.exitFunc);
